"cli.help" = "LidKeep — control MacBook sleep behavior\nUsage: lidkeep <command>\n  status                 Read current power/display/lid state\n  doctor                 Read environment and installation diagnostics\n  on                     Disable sleep, including lid sleep\n  restore | off          Allow system sleep (does not restore idle timers)\n  restore-system         Restore the snapshot from before LidKeep changes\n  ac-awake               Set AC idle sleep to never\n  battery-awake          Set battery idle sleep to never\n  ac-sleep [minutes]     Set AC idle sleep (0, 1, 5, 10, 30)\n  battery-sleep [minutes] Set battery idle sleep (0, 1, 5, 10, 30)\n  help                   Show this help\n0 means immediate lock sleep in the GUI; the system idle timer is 1 minute.\nKeep the app running for screen-lock and display-disconnect policies.\nQuitting does not restore settings; use restore-system before uninstalling.";
